  "summary": "Kukai (Kobo Daishi), born in Sanuki Province in 774, was a scholar-monk who founded Shingon Buddhism in Japan. He travelled to China in 804–806, then established a base for esoteric teaching on Mount Koya in 819. He died in 835 and his mausoleum stands at Mount Koya.",
